  "interpretation": "Base rate is high (98% self-consistent), so AUROC (suspect discrimination) is the headline metric, not ECE. conf_v0 = raw KK score (naive agent that equates 'KK-valid' with 'trustworthy'); it CANNOT separate the 4 physical bad points (they pass KK at 0.93-0.95). conf_v1 keeps normal points == KK but lowers confidence only on significant local log-sigma jumps (>0.2 dex), which raises AUROC and lowers Brier. Honesty: v1 ECE may rise slightly because penalising bad points makes the mean confidence under-confident against the 98% base rate; this is expected and reported, not hidden. Label is isotonic-monotonicity self-consistency (transport-only proxy), NOT an independent-replication hit. Small N (~6 curves, 241 pts): v0 estimate."
